{"type":"text","text":"Done. Summary of sheet 2 — the SMB enemy sprite layout table:\n\n**The table.** `read_memory` at prgRom 0x673E–0x683F (with margin read on both sides) shows a clean run of **43 six-byte rows** on a fixed 6-byte grid. The note's bounds were close: the first row is **0x673E** (the first 6-byte group after the code ending `JMP $EB64` at 0x673B–0x673D) and the last is **0x683A** (0x683E onward is `0C 0C 00 0C 0C A8…`, not a sprite form).\n\n**Naming method.** Each row was drawn as one 2×3 metasprite with `view_tiles(tiles=row, columns=2)` in the enemy palettes. The rows assemble into coherent enemy frames: Goomba (0x6792 = FC FC 70 71 72 73), Koopa Troopa (0x674A = FC A5 A6 A7 A8 A9), plus Cheep Cheep, Spiny, Buzzy Beetle, Piranha Plant, Hammer Bro, Blooper, Koopa shell, Lakitu, Podoboo, Bullet Bill, squashed Goomba, and score-popup forms. Full row-by-row list and per-row bytes are in the recorded note (Goomba, squashed Goomba and Koopa rows are confirmed by known tile usage; the rest are shape identifications).\n\n**Proof (hack `eval-sheet2-rows-a`).** Ledgered `write_memory` at prgRom 0x6792 replacing the Goomba's row with the Koopa row, then `reset_emulator` and Start/Start to World 1-1. At the first Goomba, `list_sprites` decoded OAM slots 34–39 as **FC/A5/A7/A6/A9/A8** (chr 165/252/167/166/169/168) instead of FC FC 70 71 72 73 — the Goomba was drawn with the Koopa's tiles. `undo_edit` seq 1 restored 0x6792 = FC FC 70 71 72 73, and `use_hack default` returned the emulator.\n\n**Recorded and promoted.** The note `enemy sprite layout rows` (id `enemy sprite layout rows`) now carries every row, the first/last row, and `rom_origins` = prgRom 0x673E, length 0x102; `promote_mappings` saved it (1 discovery promoted)."}
